e":false,"mirrors":7,"up_mirrors":0,"has_profile":true,"blurb":"Everest is a ransomware group active since at least December 2020, known for its double-extortion tactics. The group initially operated as a typical ransomware outfit, encrypting files with strong cr…","meta":"Everest is a ransomware group active since at least December 2020, known for its double-extortion tactics. The group initially operated as a typical ransomware outfit, encrypting files with strong cryptography and appending victim-specific extensions, but later shifted toward pure data extortion—threatening to sell or release stolen data without necessarily deploying encryption. Everest targets a wide range of sectors, including government, healthcare, manufacturing, and IT services, with confirmed victims in North America, Europe, and Asia. Initial access vectors include exploitation of vulnerable public-facing applications, phishing campaigns, and credential theft for remote access services. The group maintains a Tor-based leak site to publish stolen information and advertise access to compromised networks.","meta_source":"Ransomlook group profile (abridged, screen bytes omitted)","mirrors_detail":[{"fqdn":"ransomocmou6mnbquqz44ewosbkjk3o5qjsl3orawojexfook2j7esad.onion","title":"","available":false,"updated":"2026-09-11 21:02:02.327","version":3},{"fqdn":"ransomoefralti2zh5nrv7iqybp3d5b4a2eeecz5yjosp7ggbepj7iyd.onion","title":"Everest Group","available":false,"updated":"2025-01-20 07:32:07.300","version":3},{"fqdn":"2vqamwfdpis5rkjtpkutigykp56n6hkxfurm6qukdxp6uz5uff5kkaid.onion","title":"Index of /","available":false,"updated":"2025-03-25 08:15:49.198","version":0},{"fqdn":"bifpwatchoxp7tsb2kpes37b23ogjrb2kj4wgr7yncf4hhgsfahu7jad.onion","title":"404 Not Found","available":false,"updated":"2025-02-02 17:00:04.724","version":3},{"fqdn":"aihvh6j6fbkfjyc6jqbsh2ed4s3rym2v2pu6kd3z3exdso2xc2qwcuqd.onion","title":"Index of /","available":false,"updated":"2025-03-25 08:09:30.324","version":3},{"fqdn":"gx